stability of the Kerr black hole, J. Math. Phys. 30 (1989), 1301– 1305."}],"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/267337"}},{"reference":{"label":"60","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"24","page_end":"738","year":1970,"page_start":"737","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.Lett."},"misc":["Effective potential for even-parity Regge-Wheeler gravitational perturbation equations"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Zerilli, F.J."}]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[60] F. J. Zerilli, Effective potential for even-parity Regge-Wheeler gravitational perturbation equations, Phys. Rev. Lett., 24 (1970), pp. 737–738."}],"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/61120"}}],"number_of_pages":907,"legacy_creation_date":"2017-11-22","preprint_date":"2017-11-20","author_count":2,"public_notes":[{"source":"arXiv","value":"907 pages. The previous version was intended to be the first in a\n  sequence of three papers. This new version provides a full, comprehensive,\n  proof of the stability of Schwarzschild. It also revamps considerably the\n  material presented in the first version and provides a stronger result"}],"earliest_date":"2017-11-20","facet_author_name":["2133496_Jeremie Szeftel","1050880_Sergiu Klainerman"],"license":[{"license":"arXiv nonexclusive-distrib 1.0","material":"preprint","url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/"},{"imposing":"arXiv","url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/"}],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:1637357","updated":"2023-03-07T04:13:12.640294"},"arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["gr-qc","math-ph","math.AP","math.MP"],"value":"1711.07597"}],"referenced_authors_bais":["P.K.Hung.1","V.Moncrief.1","D.Gajic.1","R.P.Geroch.1","A.Soffer.1","P.Blue.2","Mu.Tao.Wang.1","C.V.Vishveshwara.1","J.M.M.Senovilla.1","S.Aretakis.1","F.J.Zerilli.1","S.A.Teukolsky.1","G.Holzegel.1","A.G.Shah.1","W.H.Press.1","Y.Shlapentokh.Rothman.1","A.Vasy.1","S.Aksteiner.1","J.Keller.5","Y.Angelopoulos.1","M.Dafermos.1","Si.Yuan.Ma.1","Lars.Andersson.1","P.Hintz.1","Marc.Mars.1","N.P.Pitjev.1","E.V.Pitjeva.2","T.Backdahl.1","Y.Choquet.Bruhat.1","I.Rodnianski.1","B.F.Whiting.1","R.M.Wald.1"],"figures":[{"filename":"spacetimepicturenew.png","caption":"The GCM admissible space-time $\\mathcal{M}$","source":"arxiv","key":"50368360278846695e7ea4ae75aa715e","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/50368360278846695e7ea4ae75aa715e"},{"filename":"penrosediagramconclusion.png","caption":"The Penrose diagram of the space-time $\\mathcal{M}$","source":"arxiv","key":"32bf3043e7c113844634ea384f756247","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/32bf3043e7c113844634ea384f756247"},{"filename":"initialdatalayerfigure.png","caption":"The initial data layer $\\LL_0$","source":"arxiv","key":"b70f91764b3e849e7728ccb5dee0bcc8","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/b70f91764b3e849e7728ccb5dee0bcc8"}],"legacy_version":"20181226194035.0","inspire_categories":[{"term":"Gravitation and Cosmology"},{"term":"Math and Math Physics"}],"urls":[{"description":"Quanta Magazine article","value":"https://www.quantamagazine.org/to-test-einsteins-equations-poke-a-black-hole-20180308/"}],"first_author":{"full_name":"Klainerman, Sergiu","last_name":"Klainerman","first_name":"Sergiu","recid":1050880},"control_number":1637357,"document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Klainerman:2017nrb"],"abstracts":[{"source":"arXiv","value":"We prove the nonlinear stability of the Schwarzschild spacetime under axially symmetric polarized perturbations, i.e. solutions of the Einstein vacuum equations for asymptotically flat $1+3$ dimensional Lorentzian metrics which admit a hypersurface orthogonal spacelike Killing vectorfield with closed orbits. While building on the remarkable advances made in last 15 years on establishing quantitative linear stability, the paper introduces a series of new ideas among which we emphasize the general covariant modulation (GCM) procedure which allows us to construct, dynamically, the center of mass frame of the final state. The mass of the final state itself is tracked using the well known Hawking mass relative to a well adapted foliation itself connected to the center of mass frame. Our work here is the first to prove the nonlinear stability of Schwarzschild in a restricted class of nontrivial perturbations. To a large extent, the restriction to this class of perturbations is only needed to ensure that the final state of evolution is another Schwarzschild space. We are thus confident that our procedure may apply in a more general setting.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"primary_arxiv_category":["gr-qc"],"titles":[{"source":"arXiv","title":"Global Nonlinear Stability of Schwarzschild Spacetime under Polarized Perturbations"}],"curated":false}},{"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1474124?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1474124?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1474124?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1474124?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1474124?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1474124?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A1474124"},"created":"2016-07-07T00:00:00+00:00","id":"1474124","updated":"2023-10-03T08:52:05.641346+00:00","metadata":{"citation_count":45,"publication_info":[{"journal_volume":"115","page_end":"109","year":2020,"journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214449"},"page_start":"27","journal_issue":"1","journal_title":"J.Diff.Geom."}],"citation_count_without_self_citations":45,"authors":[{"full_name_unicode_normalized":"wang, qian","full_name":"Wang, Qian","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1928563"},"ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"R.Q.Wang.1"}],"last_name":"Wang","signature_block":"WANGq","uuid":"90c57247-bdcc-45a2-ad7b-bed0b3a72301","first_name":"Qian","recid":1928563}],"citeable":true,"$schema":"https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json","references":[{"reference":{"label":"1","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"41","artid":"1993","page_start":"1993","journal_title":"Princeton Math.Ser."},"misc":["The Global Nonlinear Stability of Minkowski Space"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Christodoulou, D."},{"full_name":"Klainerman, S."}]}},{"reference":{"label":"2","publication_info":{"year":2007},"misc":["The Formation of Shocks in 3-Dimensional Fluids, EMS Monographs in Mathematics, European Mathematical Society, Zürich,. viii+992 pp"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Christodoulou, D."}]}},{"reference":{"label":"3","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"214","page_end":"189","year":2000,"page_start":"137","journal_title":"Commun.Math.Phys."},"misc":["Scalar curvature deformation and a gluing construction for the Einstein constraint equations"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Corvino, J."}]}},{"reference":{"label":"4","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"19","page_end":"L79","year":2002,"page_start":"L71","journal_title":"Class.Quant.Grav."},"misc":["Existence of non-trivial, vacuum, asymptotically simple spacetimes"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Chruciel, P.T."},{"full_name":"Delay, E."}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/584147"}},{"reference":{"label":"5","misc":["Riemannian Geometry. Birkhuser Boston, Inc., Boston, MA"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Do Carmo, M."}]}},{"reference":{"urls":[{"value":"http://www.livingreviews.org/lrr-2011-7"}],"label":"6","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"14","artid":"7","year":2011,"page_start":"7","journal_title":"Living Rev.Rel."},"misc":["The Motion of Point Particles in Curved Spacetime"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Poisson, E."},{"full_name":"A., Pound"},{"full_name":"Vega, I."}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/886475"}},{"reference":{"label":"7","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"38","page_end":"641","year":1985,"page_start":"631","journal_title":"Commun.Pure Appl.Math."},"misc":["Global existence of small amplitude solutions to nonlinear Klein-Gordon equations in four space-time dimensions"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Klainerman, S."}]}},{"reference":{"label":"8","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"256","page_end":"110","year":2005,"page_start":"43","journal_title":"Commun.Math.Phys."},"misc":["Global existence for the Einstein vacuum equations in wave coordinates"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Lindblad, H."},{"full_name":"Rodnianski, I."}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/636578"}},{"reference":{"label":"9","publication_info":{"year":2010},"misc":["The global stability of Minkowski space-time in harmonic gauge. Annal of Math. (2) 171 , no. 3, 1401-1477"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Lindblad, H."},{"full_name":"Rodnianski, I."}]}},{"reference":{"label":"10","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"23","page_end":"382","year":2010,"page_start":"345","journal_title":"J.Am.Math.Soc."},"misc":["On the breakdown criterion in general relativity"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Klainerman, S."},{"full_name":"Rodnianski, I."}]}},{"reference":{"label":"11","publication_info":{"year":2006},"misc":["Causal geometry of Einstein vacuum spacetimes, Ph.D thesis, Princeton University"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Wang, Q."}]}},{"reference":{"label":"12","publication_info":{"year":2012},"misc":["Improved Breakdown Criterion for Einstein Vacuum Equations in CMC Gauge, Comm. Pure Appl. Math., Vol. LXV, 21-76"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Wang, Q."}]}},{"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"1408.3780","label":"13","publication_info":{"year":2014},"misc":["A geometric approach for sharp Local well-posedness of quasilinear wave equations preprint"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Wang, Q."}]}},{"reference":{"label":"14","misc":["Global existence for the Einstein equations with massive scalar fields, preprint in preparation. Oxford PDE center, Mathematical Institute, University of Oxford, Oxford, OX2 6GG, UK E-mail address: qian.wang@maths.ox.ac.uk"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Wang, Q."}]}}],"number_of_pages":83,"legacy_creation_date":"2016-07-07","preprint_date":"2016-07-05","author_count":1,"earliest_date":"2016-07-05","refereed":true,"external_system_identifiers":[{"schema":"EUCLID","value":"euclid.jdg/1586224841"},{"schema":"MSNET","value":"4081931"}],"facet_author_name":["1928563_Rui-Qiang Wang"],"license":[{"imposing":"arXiv","url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/"}],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:1474124","updated":"2023-10-03T08:52:05.641346"},"journal_title_variants":["J. Diff. Geom.","J.Diff.Geom."],"arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["math.AP","gr-qc","math.DG"],"value":"1607.01466"}],"referenced_authors_bais":["P.T.Chrusciel.1","I.Rodnianski.1","Ian.Vega.1","E.Delay.2","H.Lindblad.1","Adam.Pound.1","E.Poisson.1"],"figures":[{"filename":"figI-2.png","caption":"Caption not extracted","source":"arxiv","key":"719580326d03f1e64d8d0169c4524003","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/719580326d03f1e64d8d0169c4524003"},{"filename":"fig0.png","caption":"Caption not extracted","source":"arxiv","key":"a2b102deb0dd1bc16fda64e29da4d136","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/a2b102deb0dd1bc16fda64e29da4d136"},{"filename":"fig00.png","caption":"Illustration of wave zone","source":"arxiv","key":"3b73b8742b4143a066132a367ab4939a","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/3b73b8742b4143a066132a367ab4939a"}],"legacy_version":"20210617080952.0","inspire_categories":[{"term":"Math and Math Physics"},{"term":"Gravitation and Cosmology"}],"first_author":{"full_name":"Wang, Qian","last_name":"Wang","first_name":"Qian","recid":1928563},"control_number":1474124,"dois":[{"source":"bibmatch","value":"10.4310/jdg/1586224841"}],"document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Wang:2016tef"],"abstracts":[{"source":"Lehigh University","value":"Klainerman introduced in [7] the hyperboloidal method to prove global existence results for nonlinear Klein–Gordon equations by using commuting vector fields. In this paper, we extend the hyperboloidal method from Minkowski space to Lorentzian spacetimes. This approach is developed in [15] for proving, under the maximal foliation gauge, the global nonlinear stability of Minkowski space for Einstein equations with massive scalar fields, which states that, the sufficiently small data in a compact domain, surrounded by a Schwarzschild metric, leads to a unique, globally hyperbolic, smooth and geodesically complete solution to the Einstein Klein–Gordon system. In this paper, we set up the geometric framework of the intrinsic hyperboloid approach in the curved spacetime. By performing a thorough geometric comparison between the radial normal vector field induced by the intrinsic hyperboloids and the canonical $\\partial_r$, we manage to control the hyperboloids when they are close to their asymptote, which is a light cone in the Schwarzschild zone. By using such geometric information, we not only obtain the crucial boundary information for running the energy method in [15], but also prove that the intrinsic geometric quantities including the Hawking mass all converge to their Schwarzschild values when approaching the asymptote.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"Lehigh University"}},{"source":"arXiv","value":"In [7] Klainerman introduced the hyperboloidal method to prove the global existence results for nonlinear Klein-Gordon equations by using commuting vector fields. In this paper, we extend the hyperboloidal method from Minkowski space to Lorentzian spacetimes. This approach is developed in [14] for proving, under the maximal foliation gauge, the global nonlinear stability of Minkowski space for Einstein equations with massive scalar fields, which states that, the sufficiently small data in a compact domain, surrounded by a Schwarzschild metric, leads to a unique, globally hyperbolic, smooth and geodesically complete solution to the Einstein Klein-Gordon system. In this paper, we set up the geometric framework of the intrinsic hyperboloid approach in the curved spacetime. By performing a thorough geometric comparison between the radial normal vector field induced by the intrinsic hyperboloids and the canonical $\\p_r$, we manage to control the hyperboloids when they are close to their asymptote, which is a light cone in the Schwarzschild zone. By using such geometric information, we not only obtain the crucial boundary information for running the energy method in [14], but also prove that the intrinsic geometric quantities including the Hawking mass all converge to their Schwarzschild values when approaching the asymptote.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"primary_arxiv_category":["math.AP"],"titles":[{"source":"Lehigh University","title":"An intrinsic hyperboloid approach for Einstein Klein–Gordon equations"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"An intrinsic hyperboloid approach for Einstein Klein-Gordon equations"}],"imprints":[{"date":"2020-05-01"}],"curated":false}},{"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1640269?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1640269?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1640269?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1640269?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1640269?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1640269?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A1640269"},"created":"2017-12-04T00:00:00+00:00","id":"1640269","updated":"2023-10-03T07:45:34.934969+00:00","metadata":{"citation_count":5,"publication_info":[{"journal_volume":"24","page_end":"1025","year":2020,"journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1212914"},"page_start":"979","journal_issue":"4","journal_title":"Adv.Theor.Math.Phys."}],"citation_count_without_self_citations":1,"authors":[{"raw_affiliations":[{"value":"Department of Mathematics, Columbia University, New York, N.Y., U.S.A."}],"full_name_unicode_normalized":"giorgi, elena","full_name":"Giorgi, Elena","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1976779"},"last_name":"Giorgi","ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"E.Giorgi.1"}],"signature_block":"GARGe","uuid":"3929531f-1c7c-4340-904e-aa11c303df8b","first_name":"Elena","recid":1976779}],"citeable":true,"$schema":"https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json","references":[{"reference":{"label":"1","misc":["Personal communication"],"authors":[{"full_name":"S., Aksteiner"}]}},{"reference":{"label":"2","publication_info":{"year":2000},"misc":["of the stability theorem of the Minkowski space in General Relativity. Studies in Advanced Mathematics AMS/IP, Volume 45"],"authors":[{"full_name":"L., Bieri"},{"full_name":"Extensions, Zipser N."}]}},{"reference":{"label":"3","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"365","page_end":"465","year":1979,"page_start":"453","journal_title":"Proc.Roy.Soc.Lond.A"},"misc":["On the equations governing the perturbations of the Reissner-Nordström black hole"],"authors":[{"full_name":"S., Chandrasekhar"}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/145950"}},{"reference":{"label":"4","publication_info":{"year":1983},"misc":["The mathematical theory of black holes. Oxford University Press"],"authors":[{"full_name":"S., Chandrasekhar"}]}},{"reference":{"label":"5","publication_info":{"year":1993},"misc":["The global nonlinear stability of the Minkowski space. Princeton Math. Series 41, Princeton University Press"],"authors":[{"full_name":"D., Christodoulou"},{"full_name":"S., Klainerman"}]}},{"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"1711.07944","label":"6","publication_info":{"year":2017},"misc":["and decay for the Teukolsky equation on Kerr spacetimes I: the case a ≪ M. arXiv preprint"],"authors":[{"full_name":"M., Dafermos"},{"full_name":"G., Holzegel"},{"full_name":"Boundedness, Rodnianski I."}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1637360"}},{"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"1601.06467","label":"7","publication_info":{"year":2016},"misc":["linear stability of the Schwarzschild solution to gravitational perturbations. arXiv preprint"],"authors":[{"full_name":"M., Dafermos"},{"full_name":"G., Holzegel"},{"full_name":"I. The, Rodnianski"}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1416803"}},{"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"1702.02843","label":"8","publication_info":{"year":2017},"misc":["stability of Schwarzschild spacetime: the Cauchy problem of metric coefficients arXiv preprint"],"authors":[{"full_name":"P.K., Hung"},{"full_name":"J., Keller"},{"full_name":"Linear, Wang M.T."}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1512767"}},{"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"1711.07597","label":"9","publication_info":{"year":2017},"misc":["Stability of Schwarzschild Spacetime under Polarized Perturbations. arXiv preprint"],"authors":[{"full_name":"S., Klainerman"},{"full_name":"Non-Linear, Szeftel J. Global"}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1637357"}},{"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"1708.07385","label":"10","publication_info":{"year":2017},"misc":["Ma energy bound and Morawetz estimate for extreme component of spin fields in the exterior of a slowly rotating black hole II: Linearized gravity. arXiv preprint"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Uniform, S."}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1618743"}},{"reference":{"label":"11","publication_info":{"year":1974},"misc":["black holes. Physical Review D Volume 10, Number 4"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Stability of Reissner-Nordstroöm, Moncrief V."}]}},{"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"1612.07244","label":"12","publication_info":{"year":2016},"misc":["spin ±1 Teukolsky equations and the Maxwell system on Schwarzschild. arXiv preprint"],"authors":[{"full_name":"F. The, Pasqualotto"}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1505415"}},{"reference":{"label":"13","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"29","artid":"1114","year":1972,"page_start":"1114","journal_title":"Phys.Rev.Lett."},"misc":["black holes: Separable wave equations for gravitational and electromagnetic perturbations DEPARTMENT OF MATHEMATICS, COLUMBIA UNIVERSITY E-mail address: egiorgi@math.columbia.edu"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Rotating, Teukolsky S."}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/75419"}}],"number_of_pages":47,"legacy_creation_date":"2017-12-04","preprint_date":"2017-11-30","author_count":1,"earliest_date":"2017-11-30","refereed":true,"external_system_identifiers":[{"schema":"MSNET","value":"4153087"}],"facet_author_name":["1976779_Elena Giorgi"],"license":[{"imposing":"arXiv","url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/"}],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:1640269","updated":"2023-10-03T07:45:34.934969"},"journal_title_variants":["Adv.Theor.Math.Phys.","Adv. Theor. Math. Phys."],"arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["gr-qc","math.AP","math.DG"],"value":"1712.00135"}],"referenced_authors_bais":["F.Pasqualotto.1","Mu.Tao.Wang.1","Subrahmanyan.Chandrasekhar.1","P.K.Hung.1","J.Keller.5","S.Klainerman.1","S.A.Teukolsky.1","J.Szeftel.2","M.Dafermos.1","G.Holzegel.1","I.Rodnianski.1","Si.Yuan.Ma.1"],"legacy_version":"20210316100132.0","inspire_categories":[{"term":"Gravitation and Cosmology"},{"term":"Math and Math Physics"}],"first_author":{"emails":["egiorgi@math.columbia.edu"],"full_name":"Giorgi, Elena","last_name":"Giorgi","first_name":"Elena","recid":1976779},"control_number":1640269,"dois":[{"source":"bibmatch","value":"10.4310/ATMP.2020.v24.n4.a4"}],"document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Giorgi:2017mro"],"abstracts":[{"source":"International Press","value":"We derive a system of equations governing the coupled gravitational and electromagnetic perturbations of Reissner–Nordström spacetime. The equations are derived in the context of global nonlinear stability of Reissner–Nordström under axially symmetric polarized perturbations, as a generalization of the recent work on non-linear stability of Schwarzschild spacetime of Klainerman–Szeftel ([9]). The main result consists in deriving, through a Chandrasekhar-type transformation, a gauge invariant quantity associated to the electromagnetic tensor that verifies a Regge–Wheeler equation. In this paper, we present the derivation of the main equations.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"International Press"}},{"source":"arXiv","value":"We derive a system of equations governing the coupled gravitational and electromagnetic perturbations of Reissner-Nordstr\\\"om spacetime. The equations are derived in the context of global non-linear stability of Reissner-Nordstr\\\"om under axially symmetric polarized perturbations, as a generalization of the recent work on non-linear stability of Schwarzschild spacetime of Klainerman-Szeftel. The main result consists in deriving, through a Chandrasekhar-type transformation, a gauge invariant quantity associated to the electromagnetic tensor that verifies a Regge-Wheeler equation. In this paper, we present the derivation of the main equations, postponing the estimates of the non-linear system and the construction of the dynamical spacetime to a later time.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"primary_arxiv_category":["gr-qc"],"titles":[{"source":"International Press","title":"Coupled gravitational and electromagnetic perturbations of Reissner–Nordström spacetime in a polarized setting"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"Coupled gravitational and electromagnetic perturbations of Reissner-Nordström spacetime in a polarized setting"}],"imprints":[{"date":"2020"}],"curated":false}},{"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3136035?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3136035?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3136035?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3136035?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3136035?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/3136035?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A3136035"},"created":"2026-03-28T16:46:17.735241+00:00","id":"3136035","updated":"2026-03-28T16:46:18.065629+00:00","metadata":{"report_numbers":[{"value":"tel-01832314"},{"value":"2017PA066179"}],"citation_count":0,"publication_info":[{"year":2017}],"citation_count_without_self_citations":0,"documents":[{"filename":"document","fulltext":true,"source":"TEL","key":"30769b20832e3efbbdde1d17f4bdcee5","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/30769b20832e3efbbdde1d17f4bdcee5"}],"authors":[{"raw_affiliations":[{"value":"Laboratoire Jacques-Louis Lions, France"}],"full_name_unicode_normalized":"xiang, shuyang","full_name":"Xiang, Shuyang","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/2329231"},"last_name":"Xiang","ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"M.S.Xiang.1"}],"first_name":"Shuyang","uuid":"aebaf936-6429-4a93-8a1a-11fabb52e4a1","recid":2329231}],"$schema":"https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json","keywords":[{"source":"author","value":"Schwarzschild spacetime"},{"source":"author","value":"Schwarzschild black hole"},{"source":"author","value":"Fluid dynamics"}],"references":[{"reference":{"label":"1","misc":["Numerical experiments for the relativistic Euler model 3.10. Numerical experiments for the relativistic Euler model 196 4.1. Introduction Contents 4.1 Introduction"]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"1. , Numerical experiments for the relativistic Euler model 3.10. Numerical experiments for the relativistic Euler model 196 4.1. Introduction Contents 4.1 Introduction"}]},{"reference":{"misc":["Homogenous